(item *)
(appearance *)
    There is a square brick here which feels like clay.

#living-room
(name *)        Living Room
(room *)
(* is in the house)
(from * go #east to #kitchen)
(look *)
    (if)(#wooden-door is closed)(then)
    You are in the living room.  There is a door to the east, a wooden
    door with strange gothic lettering to the west, which appears to be
    nailed shut,
    (else)
    You are in the living room.  There is a door to the east.  To the
    west is a cyclops-shaped hole in an old wooden door, above which is
    some strange gothic lettering
    (endif)
    (if) ~(#trapdoor is #in #living-room) (then)
        and a large oriental rug in the center of the room.
    (else)
        (if) (#trapdoor is open) (then)
            and a rug lying beside an open trap-door.
        (else)
            and a closed trap-door at your feet.
        (endif)
    (endif)
(narrate failing to leave * #west)
    The door is nailed shut.

#wooden-door
(* is #in #living-room)
(name *)        wooden door
(door *)
(* is closed)
(descr *)
    The engravings translate to 'This space intentionally left blank.'
    (if)(* is open)(then)
        The door has a cyclops-sized hole in it.
    (endif)

#rug
(* is #in #living-room)
(name *)        oriental rug
(dict *)        carpet
(perform [look #under *])
    (if) ~(#trapdoor is #in #living-room) (then)
        Underneath the rug is a closed trap door.
        (now) (#trapdoor is #under #rug)
        (notice #trapdoor)
    (else)
        You already moved the rug.
    (endif)
(prevent [take *])
    The rug is too heavy to lift, but in trying to take it you have 
    noticed an irregularity beneath it.
(prevent [push/pull *])
    (#trapdoor is #in #living-room)
    Having moved the carpet previously, you find it impossible to move it again.
(perform [push/pull *])
    With a great effort, the rug is moved to one side of the room.
    With the rug moved, the dusty cover of a closed trap-door appears.
    (now) (#trapdoor is #in #living-room)
    (notice #trapdoor)

#trapdoor
(name *)    trap door
(door *)
(openable *)
(* is closed)
(* is hidden)
(from #living-room go #down through #trapdoor to #cellar)
    (#trapdoor is revealed)
    ~(#trapdoor is #under #rug)
(#cellar attracts *)
(prevent [open *])
    (current room #cellar)
    The door is locked from above.
(narrate opening *)
    The door reluctantly opens to reveal a rickety staircase ...
(narrate closing *)
    The door swings shut and closes.
(after [leave #living-room #down])
    (par)
    The trap door crashes shut, and you hear someone barring it.
    (now) (* is closed)
    (notice *)

